[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Loot/LootTable.cs" id="1_table"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Loot/LootEntry.cs" id="2_entry"]

; Sera's rolled shelf (Phase 38L) - the game's second leveled pool, and the argument for a second one is
; the argument 38J already made for Hesk's: a pool rolled for a merchant who is here one day in five is a
; reason to catch her, not a shelf standing open every morning. Aldreth's stays the only resident one.
;
; Three equippables and nothing else, on ShopLeveledGear.tres's shape and for its reasons: a stackable in
; a rolled pool shows as N rows of one, and gold in a shop's pool is a merchant selling coins.
;
; Chances are lower than Aldreth's across the board. She restocks on a 5-day clock and is present on a
; 5-day cycle, so the player sees this pool roll a fraction as often - a generous table would make her the
; place you shop rather than the place you happen to catch.

